---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How PickLoot researches, picks, and updates the products we cover."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: August 26, 2026</p>

    <p>
      PickLoot is a small, independent team. Here's exactly how we put a guide
      together, so you know what you're reading and what you're not.
    </p>

    <h2>How we research a guide</h2>
    <p>
      We are not a lab, and we don't claim to have personally tested every
      product we cover — if we ever do hands-on testing, we say so explicitly
      in that guide. Our default process is research-based: we compare
      manufacturer specifications, cross-reference bestseller and category
      rankings from major retailers, and read through a wide sample of public
      buyer reviews to identify recurring praise and recurring complaints.
      We look for patterns that show up across many buyers, not a single
      five-star or one-star review.
    </p>
    <p>
      From that research, we narrow a category down to a handful of picks
      that genuinely differ on price, features, or use case, and explain the
      trade-offs plainly — including picks we'd steer some readers away from
      and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes these guides</h2>
    <p>
      Guides are written and researched by the PickLoot editorial team. We
      don't publish under invented personal bylines with fabricated
      credentials — when a guide doesn't name an individual writer, it was
      produced by the team as a whole, following this same process.
    </p>

    <h2>How often guides are updated</h2>
    <p>
      Product lineups, prices, and availability change. Each guide shows a
      "last updated" date; we revisit guides periodically to swap out
      discontinued products, correct errors, and update pricing language, and
      we adjust that date whenever we make a substantive change (not for
      minor typo fixes).
    </p>

    <h2>How we make money, and how that does and doesn't shape a guide</h2>
    <p>
      PickLoot may earn a commission when you buy something through a link on
      this site — see our full <a href="/disclaimer">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      That commission has no bearing on which products we choose to include or
      how favorably we describe them: we'd rather have a smaller number of
      guides we stand behind than a larger number padded with picks that don't
      belong.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot something inaccurate or out of date — a discontinued
      product, a wrong spec, a price that's badly out of sync with the
      retailer's page — tell us on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and
      we'll look into it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
